   "reading": "Until the unit is free again, real ambulances spend a median of 41\u201343 min at the hospital; the lab's handover draw has a median of 13.9. The handover step itself looks right: in Riverside County 21% of ambulance ED visits were held over 30 min, and the lab gives 22%. What the lab leaves out is the time after handover (cleaning, restocking, paperwork): it frees the unit the moment the handover ends, so it under-states how long hospitals tie up units."
